### 6. Build and Deploy to LG TV

Once you have placed these files in `app/`, run the following commands on your Arch Linux system:

```bash
cd /home/prem/webos-projects/cinejoy-webos

# 1. Package unified app and on-device Node 12 JS service
ares-package -o dist --no-minify app/ services/com.cinejoy.tv.service/

# 2. Install directly onto your LG 32LR686BPSA television
ares-install -d lg-tv dist/com.cinejoy.tv_1.0.0_all.ipk

# 3. Launch on the TV
ares-launch -d lg-tv com.cinejoy.tv
```

### Result:
- The app launches with the **TheBoringTV** visual hierarchy: cinematic dark layout, live TMDB backdrop transitions as you navigate through titles, smooth D-pad card horizontal rows, and left menu rail.
- When an item is selected, the application calls the on-device `http://127.0.0.1:8088` service to resolve and stream video natively, retaining 100% independence from your laptop.
